sabled-click check","comments":0,"category":"Show and tell","created_at":"2026-11-10T03:13:47Z"},{"number":2517,"title":"help","comments":0,"category":"Help","created_at":"2026-11-10T01:59:18Z"},{"number":2364,"title":"Publish a schema for --json output and MCP tool results (outputSchema)","comments":1,"category":"Ideas","created_at":"2026-11-03T09:08:21Z"},{"number":2366,"title":"Feature request: configurable paths and ports for daemon, Chrome CDP and stream server (for OS-sandboxed use)","comments":0,"category":"Ideas","created_at":"2026-11-03T06:41:24Z"},{"number":2306,"title":"Feature idea: opt-in CDP Runtime instrumentation for browsing vs debugging","comments":0,"category":"Ideas","created_at":"2026-11-02T23:35:44Z"},{"number":2314,"title":"Feature: network route --delay <ms> to hold a matching request before continuing, aborting, or fulfilling it","comments":0,"category":"Ideas","created_at":"2026-11-01T09:54:17Z"}],"latest_release":{"name":"v0.43.0","tag":"v0.43.0","published_at":"2026-11-12T23:09:31Z","body":"\n### New Features\n\n- Added **snapshot hints** for controls whose accessible name is empty or shared with another ref in the same snapshot. The hint follows the ref and lists the control's icon, image file, `data-testid`, `name` or `id`, and the text of the nearest row or list item (#2578)\n- Added a **Modern Web Guidance skill** that retrieves Chrome's guidance for a task and checks the built page in agent-browser (#2577)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Fixed **commands on closed tabs** waiting for the timeout. A command whose tab closes before Chrome answers now fails with `Target closed: CDP session <id> detached` (#2576)\n- Fixed **recordings with an emulated device scale**, which now capture at full density by switching to screenshots when a screencast frame is below the page's scale (#2572)\n\n### Improvements\n\n- Native binaries now ship as **per-platform packages**, so an install downloads only the binary for the host platform, and the global command links to it when install scripts are blocked (#2150)\n- **Snapshots of large pages** parse the accessibility tree once, so they finish sooner (#2509)\n\n### Documentation\n\n- Added a **Modern Web Guidance** guide to the docs (#2546, #2573, #2575)\n\n### Contributors\n\n- @ctate\n- @lahfir\n- @shuding\n\n","is_prerelease":false},"readme":true,"readme_zh":false,"news":[{"title":"Show HN: Skill that lets Claude Code/Codex spin up VMs and GPUs","url":"https://cloudrouter.dev/","hn":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47006393","source":"Hacker News","lang":"en","date":"2026-02-13","points":138,"comments":36},{"title":"Show HN: Smooth CLI – Token-efficient browser for AI agents","url":"https://docs.smooth.sh/cli/overview","hn":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46901233","source":"Hacker News","lang":"en","date":"2026-02-05","points":109,"comments":74},{"title":"Agent-Browser by Vercel Labs","url":"https://github.com/vercel-labs/agent-browser","hn":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46755345","source":"Hacker News","lang":"en","date":"2026-01-25","points":2,"comments":0},{"title":"Agent-browser by Vercel: Browser automation CLI for AI agents","url":"https://github.com/vercel-labs/agent-browser","hn":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46598611","source":"Hacker News","lang":"en","date":"2026-01-13","points":2,"comments":0},{"title":"Headless browser automation CLI for AI agents from Vercel","url":"https://github.com/vercel-labs/agent-browser","hn":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46587783","source":"Hacker News","lang":"en","date":"2026-01-12","points":2,"comments":0},{"title":"AgentR launches Webcmd, open-source browser infrastructure that lets AI agents learn a website once","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","source":"markets.businessinsider.com","lang":"en","date":"2026-10-09"},{"title":"浅谈 AI 进化史","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiVkFVX3lxTE5hNHY3NGRTVFVMN19WUUlodXAxSm43c0tCbm9LNnZFeURkYTFhOFdJUXVKSFdlYktFbExSQ3lfMVFmaHlMZ1AtazRrRkdFNk5U